this has been an unprecedented election  especially when considering a number of  people  that voted before polling day many of  them  by post and now a federal judge in  washington dc  has ordered a sweep of 12 postal  districts  in a bid to track down undelivered  mail-in ballots  the u.s postal service estimates that  around 300  000 ballots it's processed have not  actually been scanned  at ballot counting locations voters  rights activists  say slow delivery is plaguing some key  swing districts  they say some ballots could be sitting  uncounted at postal facilities  around the country well kristen salumi  joins us live now from  pittsburgh so there are concerns that  some ballots may be  overlooked which could potentially be  really important tell us more  yes in philadelphia pennsylvania where i  am is one of those districts where the  judge  ordered a sweep to look for those  missing ballots  you have to remember that there is an  unprecedented number of mail-in ballots  being requested for this election and  uh this is something new as a result of  the coronavirus people voting by mail  and changes to many states  election systems allowing them to do so  here in pennsylvania  three million mail-in ballots have been  requested  about three-quarters of them have been  returned  but the state does not allow those  ballots to be counted  until election day starting on election  day and some counties have said that  they will not even begin to start  counting them until tomorrow  so this has been an issue for president  trump who's called the legitimacy of  those ballots into question  and he's also questioned  another state court ruling here in  pennsylvania which  allows the boat votes to be accepted up  to three days after the election  he said that that's something that  shouldn't be allowed he's made a big  complaint about this said it will lead  to violence and so on but  you know i have to say there's been a  lot of enthusiasm here among voters  the polling station behind me is a bit  quiet now but people had lined up  early in the day before the place  opened up and i spoke to some of the  voters out there and they said they came  out specifically  because of those concerns and wanted to  make sure that their votes are indeed  counted  have a listen to what they said because  of what trump is threatening to do  with any of the mail-in votes that are  being counted later i wanted to do my  part to contribute to  the live vote and make sure to push up  numbers for biden that's literally why i  decide to vote live  i have my absentee ballot that never  opened with me just going to turn that  in in front  i think it's important now more than  ever so many people are hurting  uh this pandemic has caused so much  stress uh loss and  depression and anxiety and everything  and uh  this is the one day that we can at least  pump some light into this universe  and uh just holding up my torch  lots of enthusiasm among voters we heard  from some  biden supporters there i've heard from  trump's supporters here in pennsylvania  as well yesterday we were about an hour  outside of philadelphia and there was a  line  in bucks county outside the election  office there of people who  had requested mail-in ballots and didn't  get it or perhaps had  had some issue with their mail and  ballot including one woman who drove  13 hours because she didn't receive her  mail-in ballot and wanted to vote for  president trump  so a lot of enthusiasm on both sides but  we may not know who comes out ahead here  in pennsylvania for several days the  governor here and other officials are  warning people to be patient  for those results to come in chris and  salumi joining us live  from pittsburgh pennsylvania with that  development kristen thank you
 

